## 4. Database (Drizzle schema)

Create these tables with sensible indexes and `created_at` timestamps:

- `devices`: id, apns_token (unique), environment (`sandbox` | `production`), language (`en` | `mr`), created_at, last_seen_at
- `readings`: id, indicator_key, value (numeric), unit, as_of (timestamptz), source_url, fetched_at. Unique on (indicator_key, as_of).
- `signals`: id, indicator_key, level (`normal` | `watch` | `stock_up`), reason_code, details_json, as_of
- `digests`: id, digest_date (date, unique), summary_en, summary_mr, signals_json, push_sent_at (nullable)
- `playbooks`: id, topic (`fuel_hike` | `food_spike` | `water_cut` | `gold_volatility`), title_en, title_mr, steps_en (json array), steps_mr (json array)

Indicator keys to start with: `brent_usd`, `indian_basket_usd`, `petrol_solapur`, `diesel_solapur`, `usd_inr`, `fao_veg_oil_index`, `gold_inr_10g`, `silver_inr_kg`, `ujani_pct`, `cwc_national_pct`, plus food price keys decided in Phase 1.

## 5. Data fetchers (adapter pattern)

Create `apps/api/src/fetchers/` with one file per source and a shared interface:

```ts
export interface Reading { key: string; value: number; unit: string; asOf: Date; sourceUrl: string }
export interface Fetcher { key: string; fetch(): Promise<Reading[]> }
```

Rules:

- Each fetcher is wrapped in try/catch with a timeout. A failure must **never** stop the daily job. Keep the last good reading and mark that indicator `stale` in `/health`.
- Candidate sources (research the current official page or API for each, and tell me what you found before relying on it): petrol/diesel city prices (PPAC or oil company pages), Brent crude (US EIA free API), USD/INR (RBI reference rate or a free forex API), FAO Vegetable Oil Price Index, gold and silver INR (IBJA rates or a metals API), Ujani dam storage (Maharashtra Water Resources Department daily report), Central Water Commission weekly bulletin, Google News RSS for the policy-news queries "India import duty", "Solapur water supply", "petrol price hike".
- Store a saved fixture for every source in `apps/api/test/fixtures/` and write parser tests against them.
- Never scrape in a way that violates a site's terms. If a source is unsuitable, tell me and propose an alternative.

## 6. Signal engine

Put thresholds in one file, `src/rules/rules.config.ts`, so I can tune them. Rules are plain functions that take recent readings and return a signal, fully unit-tested including threshold edge cases. Starting values:

| Indicator | Trigger | Level |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Crude (Brent or Indian basket) | up more than 5% in 7 days | `watch` |
| Crude | up more than 10% in 7 days, or a retail price hike is detected | `stock_up` |
| Petrol or diesel (Solapur) | any change | `stock_up` |
| USD/INR | rupee weaker by more than 2% in 30 days | `watch` |
| FAO vegetable oil index | up more than 3% in a month and no import duty cut | `stock_up` |
| FAO vegetable oil index | duty cut, or index falling | `normal` |
| Ujani dam | below 40% of live storage in October | `watch` |
| Ujani dam | below 25%, or a supply cut announced | `stock_up` |
| Gold or silver (INR) | up more than 3% in 7 days | `watch` |

For gold and silver also store the three drivers (global USD price change, USD/INR change, any import duty or GST news) so the app can show which one moved.

## 7. Daily digest with Claude

- Input: structured JSON of today's readings, 7 and 30 day changes, signals, and up to 8 news headlines.
- Output (JSON, validated with zod): `{ headline_en, headline_mr, summary_en, summary_mr, push_title_en, push_title_mr, push_body_en, push_body_mr }`. Push body is at most 120 characters, and the first line is the most important signal.
- The system prompt must say: only use numbers from the input, never say "buy" or "sell", keep a calm tone, and mention the 2 to 4 week buffer rule when the level is `stock_up`.
- **Number check:** extract every number from the AI text and reject the digest if any number is not present in the input (with sensible rounding). On failure retry once, then fall back to a template-based digest built in code.
- Keep the Marathi natural and simple. Flag Marathi strings for my review.

## 8. Direct APNs push

- Env vars: `APNS_KEY_P8` (base64 of the .p8 contents), `APNS_KEY_ID`, `APNS_TEAM_ID`, `APNS_BUNDLE_ID`.
- Sign a JWT (ES256) with the .p8 key. Cache it and refresh about every 40 minutes. Apple rejects tokens older than an hour and also rejects tokens refreshed too often.
- Hosts: `api.sandbox.push.apple.com` for `environment=sandbox` devices (debug builds) and `api.push.apple.com` for `production` (TestFlight and App Store). Pick the host per device.
- Headers: `apns-topic` = bundle ID, `apns-push-type: alert`, `apns-priority: 10`. Body: `aps.alert.title`, `aps.alert.body`, `aps.sound: default`, plus custom key `digest_date`.
- On Apple status 410 or reason `BadDeviceToken` or `Unregistered`, delete that device.
- Provide a script `pnpm push:test` that sends one test push to a token I pass in.
- A push is sent once per day after the digest is saved. At most one extra push per day when a `stock_up` signal first appears.

## 9. API (Fastify)

Auth: every request needs header `X-API-Key` matching env `API_KEY`. Add rate limiting by IP. Validate everything with zod.

| Endpoint | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `POST /devices` | Body `{ apnsToken, environment, language }`. Upsert and update `last_seen_at`. |
| `GET /digest/latest` | Latest digest plus current signals, each with value, unit, 7-day change, as-of time, source URL and stale flag. |
| `GET /signals/history?days=30` | Time series per indicator for charts. |
| `POST /refresh` | Re-run fetchers and rules only if the latest data is older than 6 hours. Rate limited. Returns the new digest data. |
| `GET /health` | Per-source freshness and last error. |
| `GET /playbooks` | Playbook cards in the requested language. |

## 10. Flutter app

Folder layout: `lib/core` (api client, cache, theme, l10n), `lib/features/home`, `report`, `playbook`, `settings`.

Screens:

- **Splash:** logo, name and the tagline "Be ready before the storm."
- **Home:** today's headline, then one card per indicator showing signal chip (colour plus word), value, 7-day change and "as of" time. Pull-to-refresh calls `POST /refresh` then reloads. Show the cached digest instantly on open. If data is stale, show a clear banner. Footer shows the tagline.
- **Report:** 30-day charts (fl_chart), the reason behind each signal, source links, and the disclaimer text: "Trinetra shares information and signals, not investment advice."
- **Playbook:** "Worth a 2 to 4 week buffer" and "Not worth it" lists, plus crisis cards (fuel hike, food spike, water cut), each with 4 to 6 action steps. Draft the first version in English and Marathi, and flag it for my review.
- **Settings:** language toggle (English/Marathi), alert toggles, data-health view from `/health`, About with version and tagline.

Push on iOS (no Firebase):

- Add Push Notifications and Background Modes (Remote notifications) capabilities.
- In `AppDelegate.swift` call `registerForRemoteNotifications`, capture the device token, and send it to Dart through a `MethodChannel`. (You may use a maintained APNs-only Flutter package instead, but verify it is maintained first and tell me.)
- On every launch, POST the token, environment and language to `/devices`. Detect sandbox versus production from the build configuration.
- Show the notification when the app is in the foreground using flutter_local_notifications. Tapping a notification opens Home.

## 11. Deployment on Railway

- Services: `api` (Fastify, `pnpm start`), `postgres`, and a cron job running `pnpm job:daily` with schedule `0 2 * * *` (this is 02:00 UTC, which is **7:30 AM IST**).
- `job:daily` does: fetch all sources, compute signals, build the digest, save it, send pushes, exit. It must be safe to run twice (idempotent per date).
- Add a `--dry-run` flag that prints the digest and the push text without sending. Use dry-run for the first week.
- If every source fails or the digest cannot be built, send me a "data is stale" push instead of staying silent.
- Provide `.env.example` listing: `DATABASE_URL`, `API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `CLAUDE_MODEL`, `EIA_API_KEY`, `APNS_KEY_P8`, `APNS_KEY_ID`, `APNS_TEAM_ID`, `APNS_BUNDLE_ID`, `TZ=Asia/Kolkata`.
- Write a `README.md` with local setup, migration commands, how to run the job, how to test push, and how to deploy.

