## 13. Quality rules

- TypeScript strict mode, ESLint and Prettier, no `any` unless justified.
- Every rule and parser has a test. Run the tests before you say a phase is done.
- Structured logs (pino) with no secrets and no full push tokens in logs.
- Handle timezones explicitly: store UTC, display and schedule in `Asia/Kolkata`.
- Accessible UI: minimum 4.5:1 text contrast, scalable text, labels on every control.
- Commit in small steps with clear messages.

